{"title":"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the set  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3bb92b4964d3b8b1a7c2476b7d3b17effde0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, \\dots ,1000000\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />. Show that for any subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> elements we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> distinct elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, such that the sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/256547ecaae7e58b296f277a592bc41b53d12c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a + x_i \\mid a \\in A\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> are all pairwise disjoint.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/2/77241fbe336342cb4797f1122d0ab7ff2b49564e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\{x-y \\mid x,y \\in A\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />. There are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb9afb621469b9b690dd8e0d9baf665704ebbde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101 \\times 100 + 1 = 10101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" /> elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Two sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66aa7a7a25071253bc8b446712114c8e2cc81187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e5bc77e9a24ab62672a384216213313ca3a7c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + t_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> have nonempty intersection if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf56215db7df99e936abbbd07354900cc49081f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i - t_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />\nis in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. So we need to choose the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> elements in such a way that we do not use a\ndifference from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow select these elements by induction. Choose one element arbitrarily. Assume that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> elements, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776c27a5a58fb7fae0486ee342882bd85a40e154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, are already chosen. An element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that is already chosen prevents us\nfrom selecting any element from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8655fc5ae958a03eb714a45fc231ef9e29a590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. Thus after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> elements are chosen, at most\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f6ad67442e91bc017c74564b1b64a72f7486f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10101k \\leq 999999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" /> elements are forbidden. Hence we can select one more element.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO\" title=\"2003 IMO\">2003 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br />'\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202434\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 152/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 853/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 38/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4263/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.845      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.845      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17876:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202434 and revision id 291145. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}